From openbsd-alpha  Sat Jun 28 13:56:17 2003
From: Miod Vallat <miod () online ! fr>
Date: Sat, 28 Jun 2003 13:56:17 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: Re: help??
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=105680898328410

>      Where can I turn for help.  I'm trying to install OpenBSD 3.3 for
> Alpha on a Compaq DS20.  This system is listed as supported by the OS
> but after the install completes and I reboot I get
[...]
> tsp1 at tsc0
> panic: extent_register: already registered

Two questions here:
- with what installation media did you install your machine?
- how many processors does your system have? If it has two, does it boot
  with one processor temporarily removed?

In the meantime, the following trick should work.
- "boot -fl ac" at the SRM prompt, to enter UKC.
- at the UKC prompt, do the following:
  + enter "disable tsp".
  + you should get something like "132 tsp* disabled" in return.
    Remember the number (in this case, 132)
  + enter "add tsp0".
  + to the "Clone Device" question, answer the previous number, here
    132. Same answer to the "Insert before Device" question.
  + finally, enter "quit".
If this works, please provide us a dmesg of your system for further
investigation; to make this UKC change permanent, read boot_config(8).

Miod

