To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: Re: why always boot in single-user?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=105501977222329

> Hi, I just installed 3.3 on a 250 4/266 and it always boots into single user.
> 
> Is this what the 3.3 release just does, or is there an SRM environment
> variable that I need to set?

There is an SRM environment variable that you need to set, as told in
the INSTALL.alpha file.

Quote:

    You can set ROM variables by saying "set VARIABLE VALUE".
    Some variables you will want to set:
[...]
        boot_osflags    Flags to pass to the kernel.
                        IMPORTANT! For multiuser boot, this needs to be
                        set to "a".

Miod

